    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d318">

                <pb facs="0490" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/581.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Guthrie</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-24T17:00:00+09:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Negotiations with favorable prospects for the withdrawal of the Austrian war
                    vessel <hi rendition="#italic">Kaiserin Elizabeth</hi> from Tsingtao and her
                    disarmament and internment at Shanghai. If successful, Austrian Ambassador will
                    not leave. Japan seems agreeable to proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guthrie</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
